  "scope": "The density lambda_4=lim gp(Ka(m,4))/m^4 exists and 26/125<=lambda_4<=377/1320. For every m>=11, gp<=floor(377(m)_4/1320)+m(m-1)(3m-5). The seven-window bound holds for m>=7. The three-block construction gives gp(Ka(5q,4))>=130q^4-74q^3+8q^2 for every q>=1. This is partial progress on [arXiv:2604.15909v1 Problem 5.2](https://arxiv.org/html/2604.15909v1#S5), not an exact formula.",
  "status": "independently reviewed written mathematics; novelty unconfirmed; no all-parameter Lean",
